=== accelerator-shortcut --help ===
Usage: accelerator-shortcut <COMMAND>

Commands:
  show    Show a story or an epic as JSON
  search  Search the base team's stories, rendering a JSON envelope
  init    Verify the token, list teams, or discover the workspace's workflows
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help

=== accelerator-shortcut show --help ===
Show a story or an epic as JSON

Usage: accelerator-shortcut show [OPTIONS] <REFERENCE>

Arguments:
  <REFERENCE>  `sc-<id>`, `epic-<id>`, or a story or epic URL in this workspace

Options:
      --comments <COMMENTS>  Include the most recent N comments
  -q, --quiet                Print no notices on stderr
  -h, --help                 Print help

=== accelerator-shortcut search --help ===
Search the base team's stories, rendering a JSON envelope

Usage: accelerator-shortcut search [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --state <STATE>  A workflow state name
      --owner <OWNER>  A member's mention name
      --label <LABEL>  A label name
      --type <TYPE>    A story type (feature, bug, chore) or a local kind
      --text <TEXT>    A phrase the story's text holds
      --limit <LIMIT>  Print at most this many stories
  -q, --quiet          Print no notices on stderr
  -h, --help           Print help

=== accelerator-shortcut init --help ===
Verify the token, list teams, or discover the workspace's workflows

Usage: accelerator-shortcut init <COMMAND>

Commands:
  verify      Verify the token without printing it
  list-teams  List the teams the token can see, by team key
  discover    Discover every team and workflow, and write catalogue.json
  help        Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help

=== accelerator-shortcut init verify --help ===
Verify the token without printing it

Usage: accelerator-shortcut init verify [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -q, --quiet  Print no notices on stderr
  -h, --help   Print help

=== accelerator-shortcut init list-teams --help ===
List the teams the token can see, by team key

Usage: accelerator-shortcut init list-teams [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -q, --quiet  Print no notices on stderr
  -h, --help   Print help

=== accelerator-shortcut init discover --help ===
Discover every team and workflow, and write catalogue.json

Usage: accelerator-shortcut init discover [OPTIONS] --team <TEAM>

Options:
      --team <TEAM>  The base team's key: its mention name
      --force        Replace a different `shortcut.team_key` already set
  -q, --quiet        Print no notices on stderr
  -h, --help         Print help

